        'A Pt100 RTD reads 119.25 Ω in a bath, so T=(119.25/100−1)/0.00385=50.0 °C. A reference thermometer shows 50.6 °C, giving an RTD error of −0.6 °C; repeating at 0, 25, 75 and 100 °C and fitting a line gives the linearity error for the report.',
        'Tabulate loading and unloading readings side by side, plot the calibration curve against the ideal 45° line, and quote errors as a percentage of full scale; the viva usually asks for the difference between accuracy and precision.',
        'In calibrating a pressure gauge with a dead-weight tester, the standard pressure is obtained from',
        'The known weights divided by the effective piston area',
